    "end": "Beth cried. Mary had tissues.",
    "caption": "Mary packed light today.\n\nMary: 3.7 million people, a 25-hour day, one moon and a spare. Every group of friends here has a Mary. Her bag has plasters, tissues, a sewing kit, a charger for every phone ever made and, on the night of Beth's picnic, a moon. Nobody asks how. The bag has never been weighed, and she'd rather you didn't.\n\nI asked her for a pen. She asked what colour.\n\n(On Earth, the Moon is about 3,474 kilometres across. Mary says it folds.)\n\nWhat's the strangest thing anyone's ever found in their bag for you?"
  },
